Durante runtime patch for DynamoRIO 11.3.0-1.
Base source commit: 6847bb210bea0ca11d1bf47704383d6a075da490
Upstream copyright notices and BSD terms: LICENSE.DynamoRIO in this directory.
Only a returning vfork parent may reclaim its own completed child's context.
Restore interrupted syscalls before pending signal delivery can resume the app.
Restore private signal state for clone3 shared-memory children with CLEAR_SIGHAND.
Preserve matched indirect targets across code-cache removal (upstream issue #5061).
Preserve the original x87 status when delayed signal frames need extra XSAVE fields.
Backport decoder initialization fix from upstream commit c46d736f308e6e734bd0477f7b8a2dcbefb155d3.
Upstream PR: https://github.com/DynamoRIO/dynamorio/pull/7321
Backport thread synchronization signal-stack correction from upstream commit
985af57d7c3d73e7a1100d98e412584968588258.
Upstream PR: https://github.com/DynamoRIO/dynamorio/pull/7749
Bound delivery of a signal that interrupts a clean callee: the out-of-line clean
call save records the clean call's code cache address, and the signal handler
unlinks that fragment.
Translate a fault in a flushed fragment from the fragment as it was built: a
write to its region can make the region self-modifying, and rebuilding against
that sandboxes the block, so the translation failed and the fault was delivered
with a zero pc (JVM safepoint polls, BUG-006).
Clear the stale area pointer when the executable-area lookup repeated after the
lock upgrade fails: an area that was never executed from is removed without the
flush synch, and the stale pointer crashed the runtime when one thread changed
the protection of code that others were about to execute.
Decode a sandboxed block from a snapshot of its code, encode it from that
snapshot, and store the snapshot as the copy its entry check compares with: a
copy taken from the app code after decoding could already hold a newer patch,
so a block of a JIT page patched in place kept running the old code.
Set the protection of the runtime's generated code without querying it first:
every flush changed it four times, and each query read /proc/self/maps.
Keep the fragment that a signal unlinks: the handler took the flush-synch
entry points, which free the thread's flushed fragments while the thread is
still inside one, and the pointer kept for re-linking outlived a flush that
freed the fragment.
Do not queue a standard signal that is already pending into the last block of
the pending-signal heap: growing that heap in the signal handler acquires locks
that the interrupted runtime code may hold.
Hold the thread's linking lock while a sandboxed block that wrote to itself is
deleted: the thread is not at a linking point then, and a flusher could be
unlinking the same fragment and allocating from the thread's heap.
Flush the fragments of code that a fixed mmap replaces: such a mapping was
treated as a protection change, so the old code kept running.
Reserve 6 pages for the runtime's generated code: with -coarse_units on a host
with AVX-512 it no longer fits in 5.
Sandbox code while another thread changes its protection to writable: a block
built from it before the system call took the page for read-only, so writes of a
JIT that keeps its code W^X went unnoticed and the old code kept running.
Fixes from a review of these changes: recreate a flushed trace without its
regions also with a client; keep clearing signals_pending after a delivery;
report no pc for part of a clean call's context; forget the interrupted
fragment when the thread deletes it; raise the self-write deletion event after
releasing the linking lock; keep reclaiming execve'd non-vfork clone children
(i#1010); drop a pending signal only when the heap is full, without returning
-EINTR.
Deliver SIGSEGV as the kernel does when a signal frame cannot be written to
the stack: a SIGSEGV becomes fatal and another signal becomes SIGSEGV. A
fault delivered from the code cache freed a pending-signal entry that did
not exist (a crash on a stack overflow with a SIGSEGV handler), and a
SIGSEGV whose handler shared the full stack was forged again forever.

